(3452262, 480873, 60614, '<td valign="top">Great minds think alike.  I did the "Marble View of my World" in the February Free Study.  I like the blue marble.  Looks awfully cold in your world.  My world is warm.  Most people don''t like centered compositions but it seems to work here.  Next time try holding up something to try and avoid the sun glare on the marble.  Nice focus.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Great minds think alike.  I did the "Marble View of my World" in the February Free Study.  I like the blue marble.  Looks awfully cold in your world.  My world is warm.  Most people don''t like centered compositions but it seems to work here.  Next time try holding up something to try and avoid the sun glare on the marble.  Nice focus.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-03-12 07:30:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3452280, 481660, 49643, '<td valign="top">Excellent!!</td>', 'Excellent!!', '2007-03-12 07:36:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3452290, 482358, 16004, '<td valign="top">This should, I suspect, get at least a top 20.  Must admit, when I saw the thumbnail I figured it for a ribbon, but it''s let down slightly by the busy background, the quality of the lighting from the overcast skies, and the gap between the rings in the top left (might have been less so if cropped a little off the top to make it more widescreen?).  however, it''s still a great very likaable picture; the red of the spirally thing is nice and bold, the models posture and dress sense is very rock ''n'' roll and has personality, and it''s quite pleasingly contrasty.  <br/> <br/>A Weighted Scoring System ; composition + technical 2/3, challenge 1/1, post processing results 0.5/2, ooooh factor 2/3, originality 1/1 = 6.5 (rounded to 7)</td>', 'This should, I suspect, get at least a top 20.  Must admit, when I saw the thumbnail I figured it for a ribbon, but it''s let down slightly by the busy background, the quality of the lighting from the overcast skies, and the gap between the rings in the top left (might have been less so if cropped a little off the top to make it more widescreen?).  however, it''s still a great very likaable picture; the red of the spirally thing is nice and bold, the models posture and dress sense is very rock ''n'' roll and has personality, and it''s quite pleasingly contrasty.   A Weighted Scoring System ; composition + technical 2/3, challenge 1/1, post processing results 0.5/2, ooooh factor 2/3, originality 1/1 = 6.5 (rounded to 7)', '2007-03-12 07:40:54.000000', NULL, 1),
