(3472536, 482838, 5792, '<td valign="top">A good photograph in any genre will score well in the right challenge.<br/> <br/>Positives:<br/>Overall general quality is good and the blue as a duotone works well. The viewer may not be able to figure out what it is, but it looks interesting and that is all that matters. It has a ''spacey'' feeling to it. <br/> <br/>Technicals:<br/>As was said, quality and blue tones work well. Composition generally OK. Lighting and exposure are good. Nothing really bad here.<br/> <br/>The challenge:<br/>It fits the challenge and meets it in an unexpected way and probably contributed to the higher than expected score. And, of course, anything done well SHOULD get a good score even though they often don''t. In your case you were not punished for DNMC and that is why you got a better than average score.<br/> <br/>Suggestions:<br/>You might consider cropping smaller to get rid of the lower right corner. That would add to it''s overall ''spacey'' feeling. Apply spot sharpening to the lower bubbles... they are on the soft side and incompatible with the rest of the image.</td>', 'A good photograph in any genre will score well in the right challenge. Positives:Overall general quality is good and the blue as a duotone works well. The viewer may not be able to figure out what it is, but it looks interesting and that is all that matters. It has a ''spacey'' feeling to it.  Technicals:As was said, quality and blue tones work well. Composition generally OK. Lighting and exposure are good. Nothing really bad here. The challenge:It fits the challenge and meets it in an unexpected way and probably contributed to the higher than expected score. And, of course, anything done well SHOULD get a good score even though they often don''t. In your case you were not punished for DNMC and that is why you got a better than average score. Suggestions:You might consider cropping smaller to get rid of the lower right corner. That would add to it''s overall ''spacey'' feeling. Apply spot sharpening to the lower bubbles... they are on the soft side and incompatible with the rest of the image.', '2007-03-19 12:34:12.000000', NULL, 0),
