(3474219, 482131, 74862, '<td valign="top">Normally I''m not a fan of shots where the photographer has applied a duotone/grayscale etc. to all of a photo except one area (they remind me of those cheesy black and white posters of the little kids holding hands with just a rose coloured), but the subtlety of this is really working for you - it''s a great shot, and your post-processing has really added to it. The one drawback of this photo is that it''s tilted counter-clockwise slightly. Picky, I know, but as a graphic designer it bothers me. It''s the difference between a great phot and a <i>really</i> great photo.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Normally I''m not a fan of shots where the photographer has applied a duotone/grayscale etc. to all of a photo except one area (they remind me of those cheesy black and white posters of the little kids holding hands with just a rose coloured), but the subtlety of this is really working for you - it''s a great shot, and your post-processing has really added to it. The one drawback of this photo is that it''s tilted counter-clockwise slightly. Picky, I know, but as a graphic designer it bothers me. It''s the difference between a great phot and a really great photo. ', '2007-03-19 22:24:50.000000', NULL, 0),
